// surplus under rules.surplus: strict. loose judges a //declscope:shared as a
// whole. It stays quiet when any one thing under the directive is reached.
// strict also judges each declaration under a directive that is otherwise in
// use. That is a field under its type's directive, a spec under its block's,
// and anything under the file's. The fix inserts //declscope:private on that
// one declaration.
//
// NeverReportsReachable says neither finding
// is made of a declaration that another namespace reaches. That fact is the
// input reachedFromOtherNamespace, and no guard reads it. configureReach ties
// it to the paths below, as hiddenUse works in shrink.fsl. A reach shows on
// one of the paths, or it comes from a source the analysis never reads.
// Both modes ask one function, surplusState.reachesOutside.
// So the paths are the ones it tests, less exportedness. strict never judges
// an exported declaration (source == Exported). Here the paths are one
// variable, because no property reads two at once:
//
//   Spelled    another namespace spells it. Or a composite literal without
//              keys writes it, and the literal's type is exact. Or a selection
//              through an embedding or on an instantiation names it. All of
//              them are in the reference index
//   Satisfied  a method takes part in an interface contract in the package
//   Carried    an exported type carries an unexported method out of the
//              package. An importer may complete the satisfaction there
//   Converted  a struct conversion pairs it by name and spells nothing
//   Guessed    a composite literal without keys may write the field through a
//              type parameter's type set. That type set had to be guessed. It
//              reports no crossing, so it stays out of the reference index
//   Linknamed  //go:linkname or //export names it as text
//
// Some sources the analysis never reads. They are a generated or filtered-out
// file, cgo, assembly or another non-Go file in the folder, an unread test
// file, and a build-excluded file of this package. Such a source is not a
// reach path. It switches the rule off for the whole package. That is
// seesAllFiles. The Go tests pin each path and seesAllFiles for loose (see
// spec/README.md).
//
// The two findings are about one directive and one declaration under it.
// otherKeepsDirective is whether anything else under the directive keeps it
// alive. Suppose nothing does, and this declaration does not either. Then loose
// reports the directive, and strict adds nothing. The per-declaration finding
// would say the same thing again. So strict reports a superset of loose. The
// two never both land on the declaration.
//
// Five more suppressors belong to strict alone:
//
//   entryMixed      another name in the same entry is reached (a, b int, or
//                   var x, y). The only directive that could narrow this name
//                   narrows that name too
//   membersKeep     the declaration is a type. A member that would take the
//                   narrowed scope through it is reached or exported
//   ownerNarrowed   the declaration is a member of a type that strict already
//                   narrows. The type's fix settles the member. The Go code
//                   still reports such a member where the baseline absorbs
//                   the type's finding (finding.settled). That case is
//                   type_fix_members.fsl's, not this spec's
//   toolchainNamed  it is main in package main. The toolchain finds it by
//                   name, so a directive on it says nothing. loose has no
//                   such exemption: main keeps no directive alive
//   source          the scope must come from the enclosing directive. It must
//                   not come from the declaration's own directive, from
//                   exportedness, or from defaults.unexported
//
// The fix has six duties. It must bind. It must settle the report. It must
// start no boundary report on the declaration or on a member it narrows. It
// must never make loose fire. It must never leave the directive binding
// nothing. It must never leave a member's own directive binding nothing
// either (memberStatesPrivate, below). otherDecided is whether something else
// under the directive still takes a scope it could not have had otherwise.
// Where nothing does, the fix is withheld and the report is not.
//
// The first two duties and loose are judged again on the code after the fix.
// The boundary duty is stated for the declaration. The last two duties and a
// narrowed member are each one guard of fixable. Any property over them would
// restate that guard. So witnesses show them instead.
//
// One kind of directive binds nothing before the fix: restated. It names the
// scope an enclosing directive already gives. So nothing under it takes a
// scope it could not have had otherwise. The unused rule already reports it.
// Narrowing under it cannot leave it binding nothing. The fix is withheld
// there only where it would reword that report. rewords is whether the unused
// rule is on and the report reads the narrowed declaration. A block's report
// names each spec that takes its scope, for example. A type's report names
// the type and never its fields. So a field narrowed under it rewords nothing.
//
// One more case withholds the fix: memberStatesPrivate. The declaration is a
// type, and one of its members states its own //declscope:private. That
// member does not take its scope through the type, so membersKeep never reads
// it. Its directive binds only while the type is shared. Once the fix narrows
// the type, the member has private anyway, and the unused rule reports the
// member's directive. The directive is the author's, so the fix does not
// delete it. It is withheld while unusedReports, that is, while the unused
// rule is on. With the rule off nothing would report the directive.
//
// ASSUME-1: one declaration and its enclosing directive are enough. Everything
//   else the directive reaches matters only through otherKeepsDirective and
//   otherDecided. A type's members matter only through membersKeep (modelling
//   assumption)
fsl 5
spec SurplusStrict {
  enum Scope { Shared, Private }
  enum Mode  { Off, Loose, Strict }
  // Where the enclosing directive is written. The rule treats the three the
  // same. A witness per level is what shows it.
  enum Level { OnFile, OnBlock, OnType }
  // Why the declaration has the scope it has. Each value other than Enclosed
  // is one reason the enclosing directive did not widen it. They are one
  // variable and not four flags, for the same reason as Reach below.
  enum Source { Enclosed, OwnDirective, Exported, SharedDefault, NoEnclosing }
  // The reach paths are one variable. Reach is a disjunction, so no guard
  // reads two paths at once. Flags would multiply the states the checker
  // holds. An enum only adds to them.
  enum Reach { Unreached, Spelled, Satisfied, Carried, Converted, Guessed, Linknamed }
  // The shape of the entry, for the same reason. Each value is one strict
  // suppressor, or a type whose members are all quiet.
  enum Shape { Plain, MixedEntry, MembersQuiet, MembersKeep, OwnerNarrowed, ToolchainNamed }

  state {
    phase: 0..3 = 0,
    mode: Mode = Loose,
    source: Source = Enclosed,
    level: Level = OnFile,
    seesAllFiles: Bool = true,
    reach: Reach = Unreached,
    // The ground truth: another namespace reaches the declaration. No guard
    // reads it.
    reachedFromOtherNamespace: Bool = false,
    shape: Shape = Plain,
    otherKeepsDirective: Bool = false,
    otherDecided: Bool = false,
    restated: Bool = false,
    rewords: Bool = false,
    memberStatesPrivate: Bool = false,
    unusedReports: Bool = false,
    looseReported: Bool = false,
    strictReported: Bool = false,
    fixed: Bool = false,
    stalled: Bool = false
  }

  // Three steps, not one. One action with every parameter is the product of
  // all of them at every step. The checker holds that product.
  action configureScope(givenMode: Mode,
                        givenSource: Source,
                        givenLevel: Level,
                        givenSeesAllFiles: Bool) {
    requires phase == 0
    phase = 1
    mode = givenMode
    source = givenSource
    level = givenLevel
    seesAllFiles = givenSeesAllFiles
  }
  action configureReach(givenReach: Reach,
                        givenReachedFromOtherNamespace: Bool,
                        givenShape: Shape) {
    requires phase == 1
    // Every reach shows on a path the rule counts, or comes from a source
    // the analysis never reads. This is the model of the reach, not a guard.
    requires givenReachedFromOtherNamespace => givenReach != Unreached or not seesAllFiles
    // main is a function with an unexported name. So no type's directive
    // reaches it, and exportedness never gives it its scope.
    requires givenShape == ToolchainNamed => level != OnType
    requires givenShape == ToolchainNamed => source != Exported
    phase = 2
    reach = givenReach
    reachedFromOtherNamespace = givenReachedFromOtherNamespace
    shape = givenShape
  }
  action configureDirective(givenOtherKeepsDirective: Bool,
                            givenOtherDecided: Bool,
                            givenRestated: Bool,
                            givenRewords: Bool,
                            givenMemberStatesPrivate: Bool,
                            givenUnusedReports: Bool) {
    requires phase == 2
    // A restated directive has an enclosing directive to restate. So it is
    // never the file's, and nothing under it decides. Only its report can be
    // reworded.
    requires givenRestated => level != OnFile
    requires givenRestated => source != NoEnclosing
    requires givenRestated => not givenOtherDecided
    requires givenRewords => givenRestated
    // Only the unused rule's report can be reworded.
    requires givenRewords => givenUnusedReports
    // Only a type has members. A type is never under a type's directive, it
    // is never a mixed entry, and it is never main.
    requires givenMemberStatesPrivate => level != OnType
    requires givenMemberStatesPrivate => shape != MixedEntry
    requires givenMemberStatesPrivate => shape != OwnerNarrowed
    requires givenMemberStatesPrivate => shape != ToolchainNamed
    phase = 3
    otherKeepsDirective = givenOtherKeepsDirective
    otherDecided = givenOtherDecided
    restated = givenRestated
    rewords = givenRewords
    memberStatesPrivate = givenMemberStatesPrivate
    unusedReports = givenUnusedReports
  }

  def configured() = phase == 3

  def exported() = source == Exported
  def unexportedDefault() = if source == SharedDefault then Shared else Private
  def entryMixed() = shape == MixedEntry
  def carriesMembers() = shape == MembersQuiet or shape == MembersKeep
  def membersKeep() = shape == MembersKeep
  def ownerNarrowed() = shape == OwnerNarrowed
  def toolchainNamed() = shape == ToolchainNamed

  // A pass that ran and neither reported nor fixed. It may repeat forever.
  action pass() {
    requires configured()
    stalled = true
  }

  def enclosing() = source != NoEnclosing
  def usedOutside() = reach == Spelled
  def reachable() = reach != Unreached

  // Once the fix has run, the declaration states its own //declscope:private.
  def sourceAfter() = if fixed then OwnDirective else source

  // --- loose: the directive as a whole ------------------------------------
  // The declaration depends on the directive while it states no scope of its
  // own. It keeps the directive alive while it is reached or exported.
  def dependsOnDirectiveFrom(from: Source) = from != NoEnclosing and from != OwnDirective
  def dependsOnDirective() = dependsOnDirectiveFrom(source)
  def keepsDirective() = dependsOnDirective() and (reachable() or exported())
  def looseWouldFire() =
    enclosing()
    and seesAllFiles
    and not otherKeepsDirective
    and not keepsDirective()
  def looseFiresIn(given: Mode) = given != Off and looseWouldFire()
  def looseFires() = looseFiresIn(mode)

  // --- strict: this one declaration ---------------------------------------
  // The enclosing directive made it shared. Without that directive, under
  // this configuration, the declaration would be private.
  def widenedFrom(from: Source) =
    dependsOnDirectiveFrom(from)
    and from != Exported
    and unexportedDefault() == Private
  def widened() = widenedFrom(source)
  // Every suppressor of the strict finding except where the scope came from.
  // The finding before the fix and the one after it share these.
  def strictUnsuppressed() =
    seesAllFiles
    and not reachable()
    and not entryMixed()
    and not (carriesMembers() and membersKeep())
    and not ownerNarrowed()
    and not toolchainNamed()
    and not looseWouldFire()
  def strictFiresOver(given: Mode, from: Source) =
    given == Strict
    and widenedFrom(from)
    and strictUnsuppressed()
  def strictFiresIn(given: Mode) = strictFiresOver(given, source)
  def strictFires() = strictFiresIn(mode)
  // The fix would leave a member's //declscope:private binding nothing, and
  // the unused rule would report it.
  def unbindsAMember() = memberStatesPrivate and unusedReports
  def fixable() =
    strictFires()
    and (otherDecided or (restated and not rewords))
    and not unbindsAMember()

  fair action reportLoose() {
    requires configured()
    requires looseFires()
    requires not looseReported
    looseReported = true
  }
  fair action reportStrict() {
    requires configured()
    requires strictFires()
    requires not strictReported
    strictReported = true
  }
  fair action fix() {
    requires strictReported
    requires fixable()
    requires not fixed
    fixed = true
  }

  // --- the code after the run ---------------------------------------------
  def scopeAfter() =
    if fixed then Private
    else if dependsOnDirective() then Shared
    else if exported() then Shared
    else unexportedDefault()
  // The scope the declaration takes from outside its own directive. Resolved
  // here from the source, apart from widened. The model does not say which
  // scope an own directive states. It may state private, so that case counts
  // as private.
  def scopeWithoutTheInsertion() =
    if source == Enclosed then Shared
    else if source == Exported then Shared
    else if source == SharedDefault then Shared
    else Private
  def crossesAfter() = scopeAfter() == Private and usedOutside()
  // Once narrowed, the declaration no longer depends on the directive. So it
  // no longer keeps the directive alive either.
  def looseAfter() =
    enclosing()
    and seesAllFiles
    and not otherKeepsDirective
    and (fixed or not keepsDirective())

  // --- what the rule may say ----------------------------------------------
  // The property the rule exists to keep, for both findings. It reads the
  // ground truth, which no guard reads.
  invariant NeverReportsReachable {
    (strictReported => not reachedFromOtherNamespace)
    and (looseReported => not (dependsOnDirective() and reachedFromOtherNamespace))
  }

  // strict reports a superset of loose. Each finding under loose is also
  // made under strict, on the same inputs.
  invariant StrictKeepsEveryLooseFinding {
    configured()
      => (looseFiresIn(Loose) => looseFiresIn(Strict))
      and (strictFiresIn(Loose) => strictFiresIn(Strict))
  }

  // --- what the fix leaves -------------------------------------------------
  // The inserted //declscope:private changes the scope in force. So unused
  // reports it under neither mode. This is unused_modes.fsl's strict test,
  // copied by hand. Nothing links the two.
  invariant InsertedDirectiveBinds { fixed => scopeWithoutTheInsertion() == Shared }
  // strict run again over the fixed code finds nothing on the declaration.
  invariant FixSettlesTheReport { fixed => not strictFiresOver(mode, sourceAfter()) }
  invariant FixStartsNoBoundary { fixed => not crossesAfter() }
  invariant FixNeverFiresLoose  { fixed => not looseAfter() }

  // --- auxiliary ------------------------------------------------------------
  // Lemmas for induction, not claims. Nothing assigns the inputs once
  // configured. So each guard still holds of the state the action fired in.
  invariant ReachRecordsItsGuard {
    (phase >= 2 and reachedFromOtherNamespace) => reach != Unreached or not seesAllFiles
  }
  invariant LooseRecordsItsGuard  { looseReported => configured() and looseFires() }
  invariant StrictRecordsItsGuard { strictReported => configured() and strictFires() }
  invariant FixRecordsItsGuard    { fixed => strictReported and fixable() }

  // --- witnesses ------------------------------------------------------------
  reachable LooseReported { looseReported and mode == Loose }
  reachable LooseReportedUnderStrict { looseReported and mode == Strict }
  reachable StrictReportedOnFile  { strictReported and level == OnFile }
  reachable StrictReportedOnBlock { strictReported and level == OnBlock }
  reachable StrictReportedOnType  { strictReported and level == OnType }
  reachable TypeNarrowedWithItsMembers { fixed and shape == MembersQuiet }
  reachable Fixed { fixed }
  // Narrowing would leave the directive binding nothing. There the fix is
  // withheld, and the report is not.
  reachable ReportedWithoutFix {
    strictReported
    and not otherDecided
    and not restated
    and not memberStatesPrivate
    and not fixable()
    and stalled
  }
  // Under a directive that already binds nothing, the fix is offered where
  // the unused report reads the same after it. It is withheld where the
  // report would change.
  reachable FixedUnderARestatedDirective { fixed and restated and not otherDecided }
  reachable WithheldWhereItWouldReword {
    strictReported
    and restated
    and rewords
    and not memberStatesPrivate
    and not fixable()
    and stalled
  }

  // A member states //declscope:private. The fix is withheld while the unused
  // rule is on, and offered while it is off.
  reachable WithheldOverAMemberThatStatesPrivate {
    strictReported
    and memberStatesPrivate
    and unusedReports
    and otherDecided
    and not fixable()
    and stalled
  }
  reachable FixedOverAMemberUnderUnusedOff {
    fixed
    and memberStatesPrivate
    and not unusedReports
  }

  // Under loose, a declaration strict would report goes unreported.
  reachable LooseLeavesTheDeclaration {
    configured()
    and mode == Loose
    and widened()
    and seesAllFiles
    and otherKeepsDirective
    and not reachable()
    and shape == Plain
    and not looseFires()
    and not strictFires()
  }

  // strict is on and every file was read. Something else keeps the directive
  // alive, so loose is quiet. Each witness below varies one more input.
  def strictArmed() =
    configured()
    and mode == Strict
    and seesAllFiles
    and otherKeepsDirective

  // Each suppressor of the strict finding is witnessed on its own, with every
  // other one off.
  reachable SilentOnUseOutside {
    strictArmed()
    and widened()
    and reach == Spelled
    and shape == Plain
    and not strictFires()
  }
  reachable SilentOnInterfaceSatisfaction {
    strictArmed()
    and widened()
    and reach == Satisfied
    and shape == Plain
    and not strictFires()
  }
  reachable SilentOnExportedCarrier {
    strictArmed()
    and widened()
    and reach == Carried
    and shape == Plain
    and not strictFires()
  }
  reachable SilentOnConversion {
    strictArmed()
    and widened()
    and reach == Converted
    and shape == Plain
    and not strictFires()
  }
  reachable SilentOnGuessedLiteral {
    strictArmed()
    and widened()
    and reach == Guessed
    and shape == Plain
    and not strictFires()
  }
  reachable SilentOnLinkname {
    strictArmed()
    and widened()
    and reach == Linknamed
    and shape == Plain
    and not strictFires()
  }
  reachable SilentOnMixedEntry {
    strictArmed()
    and widened()
    and not reachable()
    and entryMixed()
    and not strictFires()
  }
  reachable SilentOnAReachedMember {
    strictArmed()
    and widened()
    and not reachable()
    and shape == MembersKeep
    and not strictFires()
  }
  reachable SilentUnderANarrowedOwner {
    strictArmed()
    and widened()
    and not reachable()
    and ownerNarrowed()
    and not strictFires()
  }
  reachable SilentOnMain {
    strictArmed()
    and widened()
    and not reachable()
    and toolchainNamed()
    and not strictFires()
  }
  // strict never lands on the declaration loose already covers.
  reachable SilentWhereLooseReports {
    configured()
    and mode == Strict
    and widened()
    and seesAllFiles
    and not otherKeepsDirective
    and not reachable()
    and shape == Plain
    and not strictFires()
    and looseFires()
  }
  reachable SilentWhenNotEveryFileIsRead {
    configured()
    and mode == Strict
    and widened()
    and not seesAllFiles
    and otherKeepsDirective
    and not reachable()
    and shape == Plain
    and not strictFires()
  }
  reachable SilentWhenOff {
    configured()
    and mode == Off
    and widened()
    and seesAllFiles
    and not reachable()
    and shape == Plain
    and not strictFires()
    and not looseFires()
  }

  // And each reason the enclosing directive did not give the scope.
  reachable SilentOnOwnDirective {
    strictArmed()
    and source == OwnDirective
    and unexportedDefault() == Private
    and not reachable()
    and shape == Plain
    and not strictFires()
  }
  reachable SilentOnExported {
    strictArmed()
    and source == Exported
    and unexportedDefault() == Private
    and not reachable()
    and shape == Plain
    and not strictFires()
  }
  reachable SilentUnderSharedDefault {
    strictArmed()
    and source == SharedDefault
    and not reachable()
    and shape == Plain
    and not strictFires()
  }
  reachable SilentWithoutEnclosing {
    strictArmed()
    and source == NoEnclosing
    and unexportedDefault() == Private
    and not reachable()
    and shape == Plain
    and not strictFires()
  }

  // The rule reports nothing for a pass. The leadsTo escapes this state.
  reachable PendingReportSurvivesAPass { stalled and strictFires() and not strictReported }

  leadsTo LooseEventuallyReported {
    configured() and looseFires() ~> looseReported
    helpful reportLoose()
    decreases if looseReported then 0 else 1
  }
  leadsTo StrictEventuallyReported {
    configured() and strictFires() ~> strictReported
    helpful reportStrict()
    decreases if strictReported then 0 else 1
  }
  leadsTo EventuallyFixed {
    configured() and fixable() ~> fixed
    helpful reportStrict()
    helpful fix()
    decreases (if strictReported then 0 else 1) + (if fixed then 0 else 1)
  }
}
